const PRIVACY = "## Who We Are and Scope\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how the Synthesia mobile application (the “App”) processes information when you create AI avatar videos, manage your creations, and use subscription features. The App is operated by Dominik Kistner, Stallschreiberstraße 17, 10179 Berlin, Germany (“we”, “us”, or “our”).\n\nFor questions about privacy or to exercise your data protection rights, contact dominikceo@kistner.click. Where applicable, Dominik Kistner acts as the data controller for processing performed in connection with the App.\n\n## Information Involved in Using the App\n\n- Content you choose to provide: photographs captured for avatars, text scripts or prompts, voice and language selections, and other settings needed to create the videos you request.\n- Generated and local content: created avatars, video outputs, previews, and creation history are stored locally on your device as part of the App’s functionality.\n- Subscription information: subscription status, purchase or transaction references, and subscription-related identifiers may be handled through Apple and Apphud to validate access to paid features.\n- Support correspondence: if you choose to email us, we receive your email address and the information you provide in that communication.\n\nThe App does not require account registration or sign-in, and it does not request your name, phone number, or email address to create an in-app account.\n\n## AI Video and Avatar Processing\n\nTo perform the generation you request, the App sends the relevant photos, text scripts or prompts, and selected video settings to HeyGen (HeyGen API v3). HeyGen processes these inputs to generate the requested avatar or video and returns results for use in the App. Internet connectivity is required for this processing.\n\nPhoto uploads are made for avatar creation, not for identity verification by the App. The App does not offer a face-identification feature or a voice-cloning feature; it uses selectable, ready-made voices. Photographs may contain recognizable facial imagery, and the AI service may apply its own processing procedures. For information about HeyGen’s handling, retention, and safeguards, refer to its applicable privacy terms.\n\nAlthough the App has no independently operated backend for storing your projects, information transmitted to HeyGen is processed outside your device. Local-only storage of your saved creations must not be understood to mean that AI request data is never handled by an external provider.\n\n## Permissions and Device Storage\n\n- Camera: used when you choose to take a photo for an AI avatar video.\n- Photos (Add Only): used when you choose to save a generated video to your device’s photo library. This permission is for saving content, not general access to your existing photo library.\n\nYour saved avatars, generated videos, and creation history are maintained on your device. You control content you export or share from your device. Deleting the App generally deletes its local application data, although copies may remain in exported files, system backups, or locations you separately chose.\n\n## Subscriptions and Payment Services\n\nPaid access is offered through Apple App Store auto-renewable subscriptions. Apple handles payment and billing. We do not receive your full payment card information from Apple.\n\nWe use Apphud to help verify purchase entitlements and subscription status. Depending on the service configuration, information handled for this purpose may include transaction and subscription information, an Apphud-generated user identifier, Apple’s vendor identifier (IDFV), and limited app or device metadata needed to manage subscriptions. This is not used by us for advertising tracking.\n\nApple and Apphud each process relevant data under their own applicable privacy notices and service terms.\n\n## Purposes and Legal Bases\n\nWe process information only as reasonably needed to provide requested AI video functions, save and export content, enable paid features, respond to support requests, protect the service from misuse, and meet applicable legal obligations.\n\nFor individuals covered by the GDPR, the legal bases may include performance of a contract (requested generation and subscriptions), legitimate interests (service reliability, security, and support), compliance with legal obligations, and consent where legally required. Where processing relies on consent, it may be withdrawn subject to applicable law.\n\n## Sharing and International Processing\n\nWe do not sell personal information or share it with advertisers. Information may be made available only to service providers needed for the functions you request: HeyGen for AI avatar/video generation, Apphud for subscription management, and Apple for App Store payments and relevant device services.\n\nThese providers may process information in countries other than the country where you live. Any such processing and international transfers are subject to the applicable legal requirements and the relevant provider’s terms and safeguards. We cannot determine or guarantee a third-party provider’s specific retention period based solely on the App’s local storage settings.\n\n## Retention, Security, and Your Choices\n\nContent stored by the App remains on your device until you remove it or delete the App, subject to operating-system backups and copies you export. Information processed by HeyGen or Apphud may be retained under those providers’ applicable policies and contractual or legal requirements. Support correspondence is kept only as reasonably necessary to handle inquiries and applicable obligations.\n\nWe use reasonable technical and organizational measures appropriate to the App’s operation. However, internet transmissions and electronic storage cannot be guaranteed completely secure. You can limit what you submit, manage device permissions in system settings, and control what you export or share.\n\n## No Advertising, Tracking, or Separate Analytics\n\nThe App does not display advertisements and does not integrate Firebase, separate analytics, push notifications, or a dedicated crash-reporting/diagnostics service. Subscription-related technical information may still be processed by Apphud as described above. The App is not designed to track you across other companies’ apps or websites for advertising.\n\n## Your Data Protection Rights\n\nDepending on where you live and which law applies, you may have rights to request access, correction, erasure, restriction, portability, or objection to certain processing, as well as to withdraw consent where applicable. You may also have the right to complain to a data protection supervisory authority.\n\nContact dominikceo@kistner.click to submit a request. We will respond in accordance with applicable law. Some data is kept only on your device, while data held by HeyGen, Apphud, or Apple may need to be addressed through those providers and their available controls.\n\n## Age, Changes, and Contact\n\nThe App is intended for users aged 16 and older. It is not designed to solicit information from younger children. Users should have appropriate permission to submit photographs of other people, including minors, and must comply with applicable law.\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in functionality, providers, or legal requirements. Material changes will be communicated through appropriate channels where required. Continued use is subject to the current version made available to you.\n\nPrivacy contact: Dominik Kistner · Stallschreiberstraße 17, 10179 Berlin, Germany · dominikceo@kistner.click.";

const TERMS = "## Provider and Acceptance\n\nThese Terms of Use (“Terms”) govern your use of the Synthesia mobile application (the “App”), operated by Dominik Kistner, Stallschreiberstraße 17, 10179 Berlin, Germany (“we”, “us”, or “our”). By installing or using the App, you agree to these Terms, subject to any mandatory rights provided by applicable law.\n\nThe Synthesia name and related branding are used pursuant to authorization from the rights holder. All trademarks and brand assets remain the property of their respective owners. The App is operated by Dominik Kistner.\n\n## What the App Provides\n\nThe App allows you to create AI avatar videos from photos and written scripts, choose from available voices and languages, use ready-made avatar options, reuse avatars for projects, preview results, and save or export videos. Available features may change as the App evolves.\n\nThe App does not require account registration. Some features require an active subscription and internet access. AI generation requests are processed using HeyGen API v3, an external AI service; generated results are dependent on that provider and may vary.\n\n## Eligibility and Responsible Use\n\nThe App is intended for persons aged 16 and older. You must be legally permitted to use the App and, where required, have a parent’s or guardian’s consent. You are responsible for all content and instructions you submit.\n\nYou agree not to use the App to:\n\n- Upload or use another person’s photograph, likeness, or other protected material without the permissions and legal rights required for your intended use.\n- Impersonate or misrepresent real people, fabricate endorsements, or create misleading content presented as authentic statements or actions of a person without authorization.\n- Create non-consensual intimate content, exploit minors, harass others, engage in fraud, or violate privacy, intellectual property, or other applicable rights.\n- Generate or distribute unlawful, abusive, discriminatory, or otherwise prohibited content, or circumvent technical limits or security features.\n\nIf a generated video uses a recognizable person’s likeness or could be mistaken for authentic footage, you are responsible for obtaining appropriate consent and providing any notices or disclosures required by law.\n\n## Your Inputs and Generated Content\n\nYou retain whatever rights you lawfully hold in the photographs, scripts, and other materials you provide. You confirm that you have the necessary rights and permissions to submit and use them. You grant us and the AI service provider only the permissions reasonably necessary to process your requests and deliver the requested features.\n\nYou may save, reuse, and export generated videos for lawful purposes, subject to these Terms, applicable law, third-party rights, and any relevant service restrictions. Outputs may resemble material generated for other users, and we do not guarantee exclusivity, protectability, accuracy, or ownership rights beyond those established by applicable law.\n\nYou remain responsible for reviewing generated content before publishing or sharing it. Generated voices are chosen from available preset options; the App does not offer voice cloning.\n\n## AI Processing and Third-Party Services\n\nTo generate avatars and videos, the App sends your selected photos, written scripts or prompts, and necessary settings to HeyGen for processing. This is an external service and may operate under its own technical limitations and applicable policies. AI output may contain imperfections, delays, or unintended results.\n\nThe App does not provide its own cloud project-storage backend. Your avatars, saved videos, and history are stored locally on your device, while information submitted for AI generation is processed by HeyGen. Your use of the App is also subject to the separate Privacy Policy.\n\n## Subscriptions, Billing, and Cancellation\n\nThe App offers auto-renewable subscriptions purchased through Apple’s App Store. Available subscription options, prices, billing periods, and any promotional conditions are presented in the purchase interface before you confirm a purchase. There are no separate one-time credit purchases offered by the App.\n\nSubscriptions renew automatically unless canceled. Apple handles billing, renewal, and applicable refunds under its rules and applicable consumer law. You can manage or cancel your subscription in your Apple account’s Settings → Subscriptions. Canceling ordinarily stops future renewals; access generally continues until the end of the current paid period, subject to Apple’s applicable terms.\n\nApphud is used for subscription-entitlement verification and related functionality; it is not a separate payment processor for your App Store purchases. Uninstalling the App does not, by itself, cancel an active subscription. Nothing in these Terms limits mandatory statutory withdrawal, refund, or other consumer rights.\n\n## Intellectual Property and Brand Rights\n\nThe App’s software, interface, organization, and original materials are protected by applicable intellectual property laws. Except for the limited right to use the App as intended, no ownership or broader license is transferred to you.\n\nThe Synthesia brand is used with the rights holder’s authorization; this authorization does not transfer the trademark to us or to users. Do not use brand names, logos, or other protected materials in a way that implies a separate endorsement or authorization you do not have.\n\n## Availability, Changes, and Termination\n\nWe may update, suspend, or modify features for maintenance, security, legal compliance, or changes in external services. We do not guarantee uninterrupted access or that any particular voice, language, avatar option, or AI output will remain available at all times.\n\nWe may limit use that violates these Terms, to the extent technically possible and permitted by law. You may stop using the App at any time; remember that removing the App does not cancel an active subscription. Local content may be lost when you delete the App unless you have separately exported it.\n\n## Disclaimers and Limits of Liability\n\nAI-generated material is produced automatically and may be inaccurate, unsuitable, or inconsistent with your instructions. You must independently review it, particularly before using it in a public, professional, or sensitive context. The App is provided on an “as available” basis to the extent permitted by law.\n\nTo the fullest extent allowed by applicable law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses arising from use of the App, interruptions of third-party AI services, or user-created content. This limitation does not apply where liability cannot lawfully be excluded or limited, including mandatory consumer rights, intentional misconduct, or other non-excludable liabilities.\n\n## Applicable Law and Consumer Rights\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of Germany, without prejudice to mandatory consumer protections that apply in your place of habitual residence. Nothing here restricts rights or remedies that cannot be waived under applicable law.\n\nWe may revise these Terms to reflect changes in the App, legal requirements, or services. Updated Terms will be made available through appropriate channels, and any additional notice required by law will be provided.\n\n## Contact\n\nFor questions about these Terms, subscriptions, or the App, contact dominikceo@kistner.click.\n\nOperator: Dominik Kistner · Stallschreiberstraße 17, 10179 Berlin, Germany.";

